<title>UK: SBC sets call warrants on German companies.</title>
<headline>SBC sets call warrants on German companies.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schweizerischer Bankverein (Deutschland) has issued 15 million American-style call warrants, in 15 equal tranches, on German companies, lead manager SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p>There are three tranches on Bayer AG, Deutsche Bank and VEBA AG and two tranches on RWE AG, Volkswagen AG and Commerzbank AG.</p>
<p>All the warrants mature on July 1, 1998 and are denominated in marks.</p>
<p>The warrants will be listed on Frankfurt and Duesseldorf exchanges and the minimum exercise lot is 100 warrants.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
